    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0291" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1751</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Reinsch
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-03T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1917, 4 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 26, 11 p.m. John Jay Abbott, Vice President, Continental and
                    Commercial Bank, Chicago, will sail on <hi rendition="#italic">Empress of
                        Asia</hi> for China, March 15, with full powers to conduct negotiations. He
                    will be accompanied by one other bank official and go from Yokohama by rail and
                    be due in Peking about April. Advise Chinese Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
